102
00:06:37,321 --> 00:06:42,800
From there, the oil is sent to a refinery or storage container via additional conduits.

103
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:48,280
The discharging process for the Harrier will take 30 hours to complete.

104
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:55,000
We'll have to run our pumps carefully to get as much out as possible.

105
00:06:55,400 --> 00:07:00,840
And I can assure you this vessel is going to be dry as popcorn at the end of the operation.

106
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:07,260
But even after its combustible cargo has been emptied, the Harrier can still be a dangerous place.

107
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:13,660
The power of the sea is so great, you've really got to watch the weather, because if

108
00:07:13,661 --> 00:07:18,940
you're doing full speed and the weather does deteriorate, the combined force of the weather

109
00:07:18,941 --> 00:07:22,131
hitting the ship can do a lot of damage.

110
00:07:22,132 --> 00:07:25,880
It can take steel structures on deck just away.

111
00:07:25,881 --> 00:07:31,060
To avoid accidents, sophisticated navigation tools are essential.

112
00:07:31,061 --> 00:07:35,293
On this ship, you can actually program the ship to watercourse itself.

113
00:07:35,294 --> 00:07:36,140
The navigation

114
00:07:36,141 --> 00:07:41,380
with GPS, and that's accurate up to 50 meters.

115
00:07:41,381 --> 00:07:46,760
So yeah, you just read off a dial, and there you are.

116
00:07:46,761 --> 00:07:49,520
Besides the weather and combustible cargo,

117
